Last night was a lot of fun, despite the deaths.  The lag was amazing...  especially when the big guns started the big nukes and my screen would just freeze with a huge flash of flames raining down on the mobs...  I'd start a song and freeze up and then get 2 or 3 faction messages, so I wasn't much help - the experience was pretty much just handed to me. :P<P>OK - DON'T worry about the looting.  I got a little loot happy myself last night *grin*.  "Oooohh...  Noble Blood - what's that for?  Eye of Serellis - what's that for?"  and on and on...  I'm sure that the guys who had been there before were laughing at us.  :P<P>Caustic Fluid is no-drop and multi-questing works sometimes...  The Warden of Tunare quest is difficult enough that I'm not willing to try multi-questing it just to save a camoed run into MM to ask nicely to loot something that 98% of the folks getting them will not want.  That will take 10 minutes if someone is camping that room - if multiquesting fails, I'll have lost a lot of time.  <P>Sorry, Leaff...  I asked at one point about the Caustic Fluids that were laying around and someone said that they thought you had one.  I wish I had sent you a tell...<P>Same goes for the cauldrons for the pally armor - they are no-drop.  I hear that multi-questing bard armor works, but I'm not sure it's worth losing all the time and expense that the other items represent if multiquesting fails.  <P>I will offer Eklah to go with Negma and camo us both to run in and loot these items from corpses if we can find folks that don't mind.  Ghall offered to go and help slaughter stuff, too...  and mentioned that Verser and some Preatoriate folks may be there in the near future...<P>Anyway, I've rambled about this stuff long enough and I have work to do...  later dudes.<P>--------------------<P>Michelle<BR>Eklah Dechoklah, 31th level Hugger of Tunare's Trees<BR>Brinne Strument, 41th level Chanteuse en Bleu<BR>Mortana 12th level Cleric Healer and Death Dealer<BR>Glyneth 15th l